WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:03.500
How I got started in football, I don’t know.

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:12.180
It was just . . . Growing up with the kids and playing sand lot and finally it just kind of fell in place.

3
00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:19.800
Football was unknown in Lebanon, so there was no previous trait that was acceptable.

4
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:26.300
And going to LSU, I think it was just . . . No one in my family had been to college.

5
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.600
We had no college graduates.

6
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:35.240
In fact, I was the only one that might of, of our family, that finished college.

7
00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:37.820
No, my sister then went to Southeastern [Louisiana University].

8
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:41.860
My younger sister finished Southeastern.

9
00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:48.960
So it was just, I guess, the influence of recruiting kind of led me.

10
00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:55.320
I went to LSU, principally because the coach, Coach Ben Enis,

11
00:00:55.320 --> 00:01:01.680
always came by McComb whenever he traveled to Mississippi and had Sunday dinner with the family.

12
00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:10.040
And we became a close-knit and . . . Also, they brought Coach Colonel [Lawrence] “Biff” Jones down from West Point.

13
00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:17.720
He was a coach who was a great character, leader, and an exceptional individual.

14
00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:20.620
These are the kind of things that kind of persuaded me.

15
00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:24.420
I visited several other schools, but I chose LSU.
